{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "weno3_js_upwind_D1",
    "description": "Pointwise third-order upwind first derivative along one axis from the five cell values m2, m1 (two cells before), c (the cell), p1, p2 (two cells after) and the spacing h, as the difference of two classical Jiang-Shu WENO3 face reconstructions (stencils/weno3_js_face_recon): for a non-negative selector sgn the left-biased form (R(m1,c,p1) - R(m2,m1,c))/h (faces i+1/2 and i-1/2 reconstructed from the upwind side), for sgn < 0 the mirror image (R(p2,p1,c) - R(p1,c,m1))/h -- exactly fire_behavior's Select_weno3 with its uf argument as the selector: that code swaps the window (im1 <-> ip1, im2 <- ip2) and returns (flux_m - flux_p)/dx, which is the same expression. Each branch reads four of the five values (the non-negative branch never reads p2, the negative one never m2), so the reach is two cells upwind and one downwind. The selector is the caller's business (see stencils/weno3_js_upwind_D1x). The third-order sibling of stencils/weno5_js_upwind_D1; bound per axis by stencils/weno3_js_upwind_D1x and stencils/weno3_js_upwind_D1y.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_difference",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "op:D",
      "order:3",
      "stencil_width:5"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Jiang, G.-S., & Shu, C.-W. (1996). Efficient implementation of weighted ENO schemes. Journal of Computational Physics, 126(1), 202-228. The classical smoothness indicators beta_k and nonlinear weights w_k = gamma_k/(beta_k + eps)^2.",
        "doi": "10.1006/jcph.1996.0130"
      },
      {
        "citation": "NCAR Community Fire Behavior Model (fire_behavior), develop @ eb77580, physics/level_set_mod.F90: Calc_tend_ls (case 8), Select_eno, Select_weno3, Select_4th, Extrapol_var_at_bdys. The transcribed reference implementation."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_template_imports": [
    {
      "ref": "weno3_js_face_recon.esm"
    }
  ],
  "expression_templates": {
    "weno3_js_upwind_D1": {
      "params": [
        "h",
        "m2",
        "m1",
        "c",
        "p1",
        "p2",
        "sgn"
      ],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": ">=",
            "args": [
              "sgn",
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "weno3_js_face_recon",
                    "bindings": {
                      "v0": "m1",
                      "v1": "c",
                      "v2": "p1"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "weno3_js_face_recon",
                    "bindings": {
                      "v0": "m2",
                      "v1": "m1",
                      "v2": "c"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "h"
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "weno3_js_face_recon",
                    "bindings": {
                      "v0": "p2",
                      "v1": "p1",
                      "v2": "c"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "apply_expression_template",
                    "args": [],
                    "name": "weno3_js_face_recon",
                    "bindings": {
                      "v0": "p1",
                      "v1": "c",
                      "v2": "m1"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "h"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
